{"name":"Scorpion","hex":"#6a6466","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scorpion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The constellation and zodiacal sign Scorpius."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone with the Scorpio star sign."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scorpion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scorpion","blocks":[{"text":"Scorpions are predatory arachnids with eight legs, a pair of grasping pincers and a narrow, segmented tail, often carried in a characteristic forward curve over the back and always ending with a stinger. The evolutionary history of scorpions goes back to the Silurian Period, approximately 430 million years ago. They mainly live in deserts but have adapted to a wide range of environmental conditions, and can be found on all continents except Antarctica. There are over 2,500 described species, with 22 extant (living) families recognized to date. Their taxonomy is being revised to account for 21st-century genomic studies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Scorpion_Photograph_By_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg/330px-Scorpion_Photograph_By_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scorpion","wikidata":"Q19125"},{"title":"Scorpion (Drake album)","blocks":[{"text":"Scorpion is the fifth studio album by Canadian rapper Drake. It was released on June 29, 2018, by Cash Money Records, Republic Records, and Young Money Entertainment. Scorpion is a double album consisting of 25 tracks. Its first disc is primarily hip hop, while its second disc has been described as R&B and pop. It was executive produced by Drake, alongside frequent collaborator 40 and manager Oliver El-Khatib. Scorpion features guest appearances from Jay-Z and Ty Dolla Sign, as well as posthumous appearances from Michael Jackson and Static Major."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/Scorpion_by_Drake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scorpion_(Drake_album)","wikidata":"Q55146346"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Scorpiones_distribution.png/500px-Scorpiones_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Scorpiones_distribution.png/1280px-Scorpiones_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Scorpiones_distribution.png/500px-Scorpiones_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScorpiones_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg/500px-Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg/1280px-Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg/500px-Palaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossil of Palaeophonus nuncius, a Silurian scorpion from Sweden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APalaeophonus_nuncius_NRM_PAL_Ar0032235.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Live_Eukoenenia_spelaea_in_its_cave_habitat.png/500px-Live_Eukoenenia_spelaea_in_its_cave_habitat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/